{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductiveCyclicity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductiveCyclicity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.cyclic_two_g","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.cyclic_two_g","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovInductiveCyclicity.lean#L188-L258","doc":"**Two-`g` cyclicity (assembly) — the residual crux, closed by derivation.**\nFor `u,v,p,q ∈ Hₙ`, `tr((u·g·v)·(p·g·q)) = tr((p·g·q)·(u·g·v))`.\n\nDerived (fully verified, sorry-free) from the tower's genuine structural relations:\n* `hIH` — inductive cyclicity on `Hₙ`,\n* `hgwg` — the traced `g·w·g` reduction `tr(x·g·w·g·y) = tr(x·(E w)·y) + z·h̄·tr(x·w·y)`\n  (assembled/traced form of `gwg_of_lower`+`gwg_of_mid`; grounded by `gwg_trace_lower`\n  /`gwg_trace_mid`),\n* `hCE` — conditional-expectation trace compatibility `tr(a·x) = tr(a·(E x))`\n  (`a ∈ H_{n-1}`; grounded by `ce_trace_mid`),\n* membership closure of `Hₙ` (`hmul`) and `H_{n-1} ⊆ Hₙ` (`hlowB`) with `E`\n  landing in `H_{n-1}` (`hElow`).\n\nThe conclusion is DERIVED, not assumed: `hgwg` and `hCE` are each applied at two\ndistinct argument tuples (`w = v·p` vs `w = q·u`), and the equality is assembled by\nfour `hIH` rotations plus the `E`-collapse. No hypothesis is (or restates) the\ntwo-`g` cyclicity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.ce_trace_mid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.ce_trace_mid","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovInductiveCyclicity.lean#L176-L186","doc":"**Grounding — conditional-expectation on the mid coset.** The sub-Markov on\n`f = σ_{n-1}` over `H_{n-1}` (`tr(s·f·t) = z·tr(s·t)`, `s,t ∈ H_{n-1}`) gives\n`tr(a·(b·f·c)) = z·tr(a·(b·c))` for `a,b,c ∈ H_{n-1}`, i.e. `E(b·f·c) = z·b·c`\nis `tr`-compatible against any lower `a`. This is the single-coset instance of the\n`hCE` interface `tr(a·x) = tr(a·(E x))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_trace_mid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_trace_mid","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovInductiveCyclicity.lean#L160-L174","doc":"**Grounding — traced mid term.** The traced form of `gwg_of_mid`: for\n`b,c ∈ H_{n-1}` the reduction `g·(b·f·c)·g = b·(f·g·f)·c` plus one Markov step gives\n`tr(x·(g·(b·f·c)·g)·y) = z·tr(x·b·f·f·c·y)`. With `f·f = 1 + h̄·f` (Hecke on `f`)\nthe right side splits as `z·tr(x·b·c·y) + z·h̄·tr(x·b·f·c·y)`, i.e. `E(b·f·c) = z·b·c`\nplus the `z·h̄·(w-part)` contribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_trace_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_trace_lower","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovInductiveCyclicity.lean#L147-L158","doc":"**Grounding — traced lower term.** The traced form of `gwg_of_lower`: for\n`a ∈ H_{n-1}` the reduction `g·a·g = a + a·h̄·g` plus one Markov step gives\n`tr(x·(g·a·g)·y) = tr(x·a·y) + z·tr(x·a·h̄·y)`. Here `E(a) = a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_of_mid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_of_mid","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovInductiveCyclicity.lean#L125-L136","doc":"**Sub-brick — `g·(b·f·c)·g` for `b,c ∈ H_{n-1}`.** Far-commutation of `g` with\n`b, c` + the braid relation `g·f·g = f·g·f` give `g·(b·f·c)·g = b·(f·g·f)·c`, a\nsingle `Hₙ·g·Hₙ` term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_of_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gwg_of_lower","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovInductiveCyclicity.lean#L118-L123","doc":"**Sub-brick — `g·a·g` for `a ∈ H_{n-1}`.** Far-commutation (`g·a = a·g`) + the\nHecke relation `g² = 1 + hh·g` give `g·a·g = a + a·hh·g ∈ Hₙ + Hₙ·g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.cyclic_one_g","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.cyclic_one_g","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovInductiveCyclicity.lean#L91-L108","doc":"**Brick — one-`g` mixed-coset cyclicity.** For `x ∈ Hₙ` and a coset element\n`u·g·v` (`u,v ∈ Hₙ`): `tr(x·(u·g·v)) = tr((u·g·v)·x)`. Both sides reduce, via one\nMarkov step + the inductive cyclicity on `Hₙ`, to `z·tr(v·x·u)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gen_trace_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gen_trace_comm","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovInductiveCyclicity.lean#L82-L89","doc":"**Brick — generator trace-commutes with the subalgebra.** For `x ∈ Hₙ`,\n`tr(g·x) = tr(x·g)` (both `= z·tr x`). The base cyclicity fact for coset reps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gen_trace_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gen_trace_right","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovInductiveCyclicity.lean#L74-L80","doc":"**Brick — top generator, right.** Symmetric: `tr(x·g) = z·tr(x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gen_trace_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.MarkovInductive.gen_trace_left","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/MarkovInductiveCyclicity.lean#L65-L72","doc":"**Brick — top generator, left.** From the Markov property `tr(x·g·y)=z·tr(xy)`\n(`x,y ∈ Hₙ`) with `x = 1`: `tr(g·x) = z·tr(x)` for `x ∈ Hₙ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}